    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">This two-part volume addresses the specific area of interdisciplinary connections within special education research.  Special education has transformed as a result of legislation, new trends and current research investigations.  Currently, there is no comprehensive resource that effectively covers these advances. Part A sets the agenda for this two-part volume by addressing the challenge of why an interdisciplinary understanding is necessary and also outlines the benefits of adopting a multidisciplinary framework</marc:subfield>
